# HealthyHires edge for local testing: the production routes, headers and CSP in front of a locally running API
# and the built frontend (App/dist). The routes and headers live in configs_production/site.caddy, the file
# Caddyfile.production imports, so ZAP, Playwright and k6 run against the same edge that is deployed (ADR-020,
# ADR-019, ADR-018). It is mounted next to this file in the container, which is why the import below has no path.
#
# Not part of everyday development — the frontend runs on the Vite dev server, which proxies /api itself — and
# not part of the AppHost. Start it on demand with host networking, so it reaches the API on localhost exactly
# as Caddy does inside the pod; see development-architecture.md §3.3 for the command.
#
# What differs from production: plain HTTP on :8088, no ACME and no metrics endpoint. Set when starting it:
#
#   API_UPSTREAM    the API, e.g. localhost:5180
#   BLOB_ENDPOINT   Azurite's blob endpoint, e.g. http://localhost:10000
#
# ENTRA_TENANT_ID, ENTRA_CLIENT_ID and API_SCOPE are empty unless set; /config.json then serves empty strings.
{
	admin off
	auto_https off
}

import site.caddy

:8088 {
	import healthyhires_site
	import access_log
}
